  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Why I'm mapping the entire food-service industry in public</h1>
    <p class="meta">August 2, 2026</p>
    <p>
      Most food operators are drowning in options. There are hundreds of POS systems, kitchen-display
      tools, inventory apps, scheduling platforms, online-ordering middlemen, and now a wave of
      physical automation — from fry-station robots to smart vending. Almost nobody has a clear,
      honest map of what exists, what it costs, and what it's actually good for.
    </p>
    <p>So I'm building one, in the open.</p>
    <p>
      This site is a living hub for the food-service industry: the software, the physical tools, the
      SOPs, and the players across restaurants, quick-serve, vending, and meal service. As I research
      each corner, I'll publish what I find — no affiliate spin, just what's real.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two reasons. First, it's the fastest way for me to learn the industry deeply. Second, a clear
      map is genuinely useful — to operators choosing tools, and to me when I help them do it.
    </p>
    <p>More soon.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
